{"archetypes":[{"name":"caller-contract","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"The plan changes design-log-publish.sh exit codes from always-0 to hard-exit-1 on post-push failures, explicitly flagging design-pause-save.sh as a risk but leaving audit to 'verify during implementation' without a plan step — a named gap that static reviewers may underweight because it lives in an out-of-scope file.","prompt_body":"Audit every callsite of `scripts/design-log-publish.sh` and any script that sources or invokes it transitively. For each callsite determine whether the caller checks the exit code, uses `set -e`, or relies solely on `PUBLISH_OK` stdout parsing. Flag callers where the new hard-exit-1 on post-push failures would propagate differently than the old always-exit-0 contract, especially `design-pause-save.sh` (named in the plan's failure-modes section as unresolved). Cross-check that the plan's mitigation — 'narrow the hard-exit set to --reason final only if pause callers cannot handle exit 1' — has a concrete corresponding plan step or is silently deferred. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"path-derivation","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"The plan derives the quiet-log source root as `dirname \"$source_dir\"` inside lib-larch-log.sh, implicitly assuming quiet logs always land exactly one level above the breadcrumbs/ subdir — but this layout assumption is not verified against the actual session-tmpdir conventions used by each skill (implement, design, research, review), which all set LARCH_BREADCRUMB_SOURCE_DIR independently.","prompt_body":"Verify that the plan's `dirname \"$source_dir\"` derivation correctly resolves to the session-tmpdir root for every skill that calls `larch-log.sh commit` — specifically check `IMPLEMENT_TMPDIR`, `DESIGN_TMPDIR`, `RESEARCH_TMPDIR`, and `REVIEW_TMPDIR` layouts and how each sets `LARCH_BREADCRUMB_SOURCE_DIR`. Confirm that `larch-quiet-<script>-<pid>.log` files are actually written to that exact parent directory (not a subdirectory) by `lib-quiet.sh` or its consumers. Flag any case where the derived parent path would miss quiet logs or traverse outside the expected tmpdir boundary. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."}]}
